    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57b7b6b5_69ba3ca4",
        "filename": "board/cr50/wp.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-20T21:03:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the idea is that the \"wp asserted\" state has higher priority, so in case something happens between lines 28 and 29, the next boot will make sure that the system comes up with WP asserted.\n\nOn the deassertion path I think it is better to first set the RBOX state and then the bit in the bitmask, so that if something happens betweek lines 31 and 32, the device comes back with writes disabled.\n\nThis all is fairely moot, because on resets/panics we don\u0027t care of these, but just in case.\n\nDoes this make sense, do you think a comment is needed?",
      "parentUuid": "57b7b6b5_c6ba376b",
      "revId": "b1d15d9e78a74bf19905180de296fcf770f0cf4b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
